@subsubsection Propfind

Provided by the module @code{(calp webdav propfind)}.

@defun exec-propfind body resource
Takes an xml document containing a propfind element as defined by RFC
4918, its implemented in terms of the below mention procedures. It
also dispatches to the methods @code{dead-properties} and @code{live-properties}.

Once the requested set is gathered, propstat objects are merged
through @code{merge-propstat}. When an allprop is executed,
``missing'' live properties (e.g. those returning 404 propstat
objects) are omitted. This has the consequence that
@code{<DAV:propname/>} requests might return properties which later
turn out to not exist.

When properties are explicitly named, but don't exist, then proper 404
responses are generated.
@end defun

@defun propfind-all-dead-properties resource
Calls @code{dead-properties} on the resource, and adds a wrapping
@code{propstat} object with status code 200.
@end defun

@defun propfind-most-live-properties resource
When the request is an @code{<DAV:allprop/>}, only all dead properties
and the live properties explicitly stated in the RFC should be returned.

This methods retrieves all properties specified in the
@code{webdav-properties} list, which is non-extendable, executes them
on the given resource, and then filters out any 404 responses.
@end defun

@c @defun propfind-all-live-properties resource
@c @end defun

@defun propfind-selected-properties resource properties
Simply calls get-property for specified property.
@end defun
